[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\path[use as bounding box] (-2,-1.5) rectangle (6.5,5.5);
\definecolor{graphgrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[graphgrid,very thin,xstep=5mm,ystep=5mm] (0,0) grid (6,4.5);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,4.8);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.3,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {1/200,2/400,3/600,4/800} {\draw[black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y); \path (-0.15,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\lab$};}
\path (-0.15,0) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw[black] (\x,-0.1)--(\x,0); \path (\x,-0.15) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(6,4.5);
\draw[mathblue,dashed,->] (4,0)--(4,3);
\draw[mathblue,dashed,->] (4,3)--(0,3);
\fill[mathblue] (4,3) circle (2pt);
\path (-1.65,2.25) node[rotate=90] {Interest (dollars)};
\path (3,-1.15) node {Time (years)};
\path (3,5.15) node {Simple interest earned};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Read up from $4$ years to the line, then across to the interest axis.
$I = \$600.00$
$\begin{align*}I &= Prn \\ \$600 &= \$5000 \times r \times 4 \\ \$600 &= \$20\,000 \times r \\ r &= \frac{600}{20\,000} \\ r &= 0.03\end{align*}$
Multiply the decimal rate by $100$ to express it as a percentage.
$\begin{align*}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}0.03 \times 100\% \\ &= 3\%\end{align*}$
The annual interest rate is $3\%$ p.a.
